Internal configuration storage
The configuration data is organized using a hierarchical array-based structure. Each configuration section is represented by a
SectionSt
structure containing its name and a dynamic array of
OptionSt
elements. Each option stores its corresponding key and value as strings.
The main class maintains an array of these section structures through the array
m_configs[]
, effectively representing the relationship between sections and their associated configuration options.
This approach keeps the implementation relatively simple while taking advantage of MQL5's support for structures and dynamic arrays. It also allows the parser to preserve the order in which sections and options are encountered during file processing and makes it straightforward to append new options, update existing values, merge duplicate sections, and remove configuration entries without introducing additional storage abstractions.
