One notable difference between our implementation and Python's configparser module concerns inline comments. Python's ConfigParser class disables inline comments by default
inline_comment_prefixes=None
, meaning comment characters appearing after a configuration value are treated as part of that value unless explicitly configured otherwise.
Our MQL5 implementation allows inline comment prefixes to be supplied through the class constructor. By default, the implementation recognizes the configured prefixes and removes everything appearing after their first occurrence on a line.
To reproduce Python's default behavior, inline comment processing can be disabled by providing an empty set of prefixes (' ").
Extracting a section
A section name is anything wrapped in square brackets ( [ ] ), only if the first bracket is the first letter of a line in a configuration file.
