Accessing Values Using the get() Method
Unlike the get() method offered by Python's configparser, which returns the value, our MQL5 equivalent returns a boolean value (true for success or false for failure). The obtained value will be referred to as the last variable in a function's argument.
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| Retrieves and converts an option value from a specified section. |
//|                                                                  |
