Final Thoughts
Configuration files are an important part of modern software development, providing a convenient way to separate application settings from program logic. They allow programs to be configured, customized, and reused without requiring changes to the underlying source code. In MetaTrader 5, configuration files are not an entirely new concept either, as
INI files can already be used to configure and automate the Strategy Tester from the command line
. These files can be useful in MQL5 applications when configuration needs to be shared between programs or maintained separately from the source code.
In this article, we explored the Python configparser module and its approach to working with INI-style configuration files. Based on these concepts, we implemented the CConfigParser class in MQL5, providing an interface for reading, accessing, modifying, and writing configuration data.
With the class CConfigParser, MQL5 programs can now work with these configuration files through a clean and reusable API, bringing another useful concept from Python's standard library into the MQL5 ecosystem.
Although MQL5 already provides program inputs and
.set
files for many configuration needs, an INI-based configuration system can be useful when configuration data needs to be managed independently of MetaTrader's input system or exchanged with external applications.
